        {
          "id": "summary_header",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "h2",
          "text": "Summary"
        },
        {
          "id": "summary_text",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "This 3-day itinerary for a family of four in Rome is designed to cover the city's most iconic sites at a comfortable pace. Day 1 focuses on Ancient Rome, including the Colosseum and Roman Forum. Day 2 is dedicated to Vatican City, with visits to the Vatican Museums and St. Peter's Basilica. Day 3 offers a more relaxed walking tour of famous landmarks like the Spanish Steps, Trevi Fountain, and the Pantheon, with ample time for exploration and gelato."
        },
        {
          "id": "assumptions_header",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "h2",
          "text": "Assumptions"
        },
        {
          "id": "assumptions_list",
          "component": "List",
          "direction": "vertical",
          "children": [
            "assumption_1",
            "assumption_2",
            "assumption_3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "assumption_1",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "- The family includes two adults and two children old enough to enjoy historical sites (e.g., ages 8+)."
        },
        {
          "id": "assumption_2",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "- The family will use a combination of walking and public transportation (Metro/bus)."
        },
        {
          "id": "assumption_3",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "- All tickets for major attractions (Colosseum, Vatican Museums) will be booked online well in advance to secure specific time slots and avoid long queues."
        },
        {
